{"case_id":"T5021","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","stateful_socket_event_processing"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["ares_process_fd","ares_process_fds","ares_process_fds_nolock","process_write"],"reason":"H0 never exercises the event-processing API or the stateful distinction between read and write sockets. The changed `ares_process_fd` logic specifically constructs `ares_fd_events_t` entries and must associate `ARES_FD_EVENT_WRITE` with `write_fd`, including when `write_fd != read_fd`; parser-only fuzzing cannot reach or validate that behavior.","evidence":["`test/ares-test-fuzz-name.c` only passes a fuzzed name to `ares_create_query`.","`test/ares-test-fuzz.c` only parses, inspects, and rewrites DNS message bytes through APIs including `ares_dns_parse` and `ares_dns_write`; its legacy branch only invokes `ares_parse_*_reply` functions.","No H0 entry point creates an `ares_channel_t`, supplies socket descriptors, or calls `ares_process_fd` or `ares_process_fds`.","The S1 change replaces `events[nevents - 1].fd = read_fd` with `events[nevents - 1].fd = write_fd` in the write-event branch of `ares_process_fd`.","When `write_fd != read_fd`, `ares_process_fd` creates a separate event whose `ARES_FD_EVENT_WRITE` bit is consumed by `ares_process_fds_nolock` and passed to `process_write(channel, events[i].fd)`."],"recommended_action":"Add a stateful fuzz harness for `ares_process_fd`/`ares_process_fds` that initializes a channel and models readable/writable socket events, explicitly varying `ARES_SOCKET_BAD`, equal `read_fd`/`write_fd`, and distinct descriptors, with assertions or instrumented socket behavior confirming that write processing targets `write_fd`."}
